  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Data Structures**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the foundational data structures for the Beyblade X Tournament application. The `Blader` interface in `/src/types.ts` is the starting point, encompassing Blader details like ID, name, and combos. I\'m also considering the best way to represent stats (wins, losses, etc.) and ensure data integrity across the application. I\'m focusing on creating an efficient and scalable architecture.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the core data structures. I\'ve designed `Combo`, `TournamentConfig`, `Match`, and `BracketNode` interfaces to represent the essential elements of a Beyblade X tournament. I\'m considering detailed battle events and score tracking within the `Match` interface, and how to structure single/double elimination brackets.\n\n\n**Outlining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI components. I\'ve defined an `ActiveView` enum to manage screen states and started mapping components to specific screens. Currently, the `Header` and `Sidebar` are taking shape, with planned functionalities like theme toggles, navigation, and quick action buttons. The `DashboardScreen`, `ConfigScreen`, `BladersScreen`, and `BracketScreen` components are also being designed, each with their own unique features.\n\n\n**Designing Match Screens**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific screen designs. I\'ve started work on `/src/components/screens/MatchesScreen.tsx`, including match scheduling and filtering, and am designing the `/src/components/screens/EquipmentScreen.tsx` for the official Beyblade X database. I am also working on the `/src/components/screens/RulesScreen.tsx` for the official rulebook, and the `/src/components/screens/HistoryScreen.tsx` for tournament logs. I\'m also planning the `WinnerModal.tsx` and `NewBattleModal.tsx` components.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 786971288
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
