  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Light Mode Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of why Light Mode feels off. Initial investigation shows inconsistencies in background colors: `index.css` sets a general background color with dots, while `App.tsx` uses a slightly different color and a gradient. This discrepancy immediately highlights potential visual clashes. Further analysis is needed to identify all divergent styles.\n\n\n**Refining Light Mode Visuals**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on improving the light mode\'s aesthetic. The current background, with its faint gray grid from the existing implementation (`800a_1px,transparent_1px)...]`), needs an overhaul for a crisp, athletic look. I\'m proposing a cleaner palette with `bg-[#F4F6F9]`. Additionally, glass panels in light mode will now have a white background with a specific border and shadow, moving away from the previously transparent appearance.\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on readability.\nExisting Summary:\n\n**Analyzing Light Mode Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of why Light Mode feels off. Initial investigation shows inconsistencies in background colors: `index.css` sets a general background color with dots, while `App.tsx` uses a slightly different color and a gradient. This discrepancy immediately highlights potential visual clashes. Further analysis is needed to identify all divergent styles.\n\n**Refining Light Mode Visuals**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on improving the light mode\'s aesthetic. The current background, with its faint gray grid from the existing implementation (`800a_1px,transparent_1px)...]`), needs an overhaul for a crisp, athletic look. I\'m proposing a cleaner palette with `bg-[#F4F6F9]`. Additionally, glass panels in light mode will now have a white background with a specific border and shadow, moving away from the previously transparent appearance.\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on readability.\n\n\n**Adjusting UI Component Styles**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously updating the visual styles. For light mode, card backgrounds are now `bg-slate-100` with appropriate borders. Input elements are updated with specific background, border, and text colors. Moreover, I am refining the scoring buttons: crimson for XTREME FINISH, amber-orange for BURST FINISH, emerald for OVER FINISH, slate for STADIUM OUT, and electric blue for SPIN FINISH, all with crisp white text. I\'ve also redefined the scoreboard\'s corner colorations, and the central target box. Finally, I\'ve defined the appearance for the Header and Sidebar, including active and inactive links.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 963334175
    }
