  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Tournament Reset**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a robust tournament reset feature. My goal is to create a modal dialog that replaces the broken button, avoiding `confirm()` or `alert()`. I need this dialog to provide clear options: \"Reiniciar Torneo Actual (Restablecer cruces y marcadores manteniendo Bladers)\", \"Reiniciar Torneo (Eliminar cruces y marcadores, eliminar Bladers)\". My current design calls for options to reset with/without keeping Bladers.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Persistence**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating Supabase to enhance data persistence. I\'ve initialized the Supabase client with the provided URL and key and created a database named \"beybladetorneo.\" Now, I\'m designing functions to manage data sync for Bladers, combos, and tournament history. I\'m exploring how to handle offline scenarios and table provisioning, focusing on a robust system that stores data and avoids the need to delete and recreate the tables if data is lost.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Synchronization**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core synchronization logic for various data types. This involves developing functions to `save`, `get`, and `delete` Bladers, Equipment Combos, Matches, and Tournament History. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of a realtime connection indicator in the UI to display the connection status to Supabase and database name. A migration helper or copyable schema will be available in Config or Support Modal, allowing one-click table creation in the Supabase SQL editor.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been defining data structures, specifically adding `weight` and `notes` to the `amina` data type. Also, I added the `TournamentRecord` type for history, including fields like title, date, season, and details about winners and match summaries to be included in our DB. I believe I have the structure ready.\n\n**Creating Badges**\n\nI\'m starting to create a badge registry. I\'m focusing on defining a rich set of badges that can be awarded for various achievements within the tournaments. I\'ve begun with some badge examples.\n\n\n**Developing Badge Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating badge functionality. The current plan involves allowing users to view, award, and manage badges on Blader profiles, as well as during match conclusions. I\'ve defined several initial badges, including \"Rey de la Resistencia\" for spin finishes, and \"Blader Verificado\" for community membership, among others. I\'m focusing on making badge management intuitive within the application.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 331211010
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
