    thinking: "**Refining Empty State Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on conditional rendering within `EquipmentScreen.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m working on how the application handles empty equipment inventories. If the `blades`, `ratchets`, and `bits` arrays are all empty, I want to display a specific message in the \"combos\" tab instead of showing the Dransword simulator with dummy data when the \'parts\' array is empty as well.\n\n\n**Implementing Empty State UI**\n\nI\'ve crafted a new UI component, an \"Empty State\" card, for the application. My goal is to use this card when the user has no parts or combos yet. I want to render it within the component in `EquipmentScreen.tsx` to handle these specific empty states more elegantly. The idea is to direct the user toward adding new items.\n\n\n**Expanding Combo Creation Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Add Combo\" modal\'s behavior. I\'m implementing logic to allow users to manually type in blade, ratchet, and bit names when the related arrays are empty. Input fields are being added for manual entry, and I\'ve also incorporated error handling within the `handleSaveCurrentCombo` function to alert the user if they haven\'t provided all required components. Finally, I\'m considering the edge case in tab 2, \"parts catalog\" if `filteredParts.length === 0`.\n\n\n"
