  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering User Requirements**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s need for flexible registration of combos within the software. The key is to make the combo entry optional, not a mandatory 3-combo requirement. I\'m exploring how to design this to accommodate scenarios with one or two combos, thereby allowing greater adaptability.\n\n\n**Analyzing Combo Registration**\n\nI\'ve examined the current system, specifically the forced defaults for combo registration. The software was creating three combos, even when the user needed fewer. My priority is to create flexible registration; the design should allow one, two, or three combos, or even zero, with dynamic adding and removal. I\'m focusing on \"A\303\261adir Combo\" and \"Quitar\" buttons for add/remove functionality. Empty slots must not be auto-populated!\n\n\n"
