  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Combo Flexibility**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `BladersScreen.tsx`. It seems rigid to hardcode `combo1`, `combo2`, and `combo3`. My initial thought is to give the user the power to decide how many combos they want, perhaps through a dropdown or even a dynamic list. Alternatively, we could allow for empty combo configurations.\n\n\n**Refining Combo Structure**\n\nI\'ve been refining the combo structure, aiming for user flexibility. My goal is to make it so that if a user only provides one or two combos, we save those. I\'m exploring selector buttons or a dynamic list for deck mode: 1v1, 2 Combos, or 3on3. The UI will reflect the selected number of combos, and I\'ll avoid rigid text and instead use dynamic labels. In the form, I plan to offer a quick selector or dynamic slots to add/remove combos. The default is 1 combo.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 735744517
    }
