  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Database Errors**\n\nOkay, I\'m now looking into the issues the user reported regarding bladers not uploading to the database. My focus is centered on identifying the root cause behind the failed data uploads, specifically within Supabase. I\'m investigating potential discrepancies between the registration process and the database integration.\n\n\n**Analyzing Supabase Function**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `syncBladerToSupabase` function. The code doesn\'t properly handle Supabase errors! There\'s no robust error checking on the upsert response, which means we\'re missing crucial error messages and failing silently. That also means we\'re not properly returning or logging meaningful information! This could be why users don\'t see status or what\'s failing. It\'s time to add detailed error handling.\n\n\n**Examining Time & Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `registered_at` field and potential data type mismatches. I\'m reviewing how the date is formatted in the frontend and the database schema. It seems there\'s a discrepancy: the front end sends a date string, but the database expects a timestamp. Also, I\'m checking if we\'re sending a large base64 data URL for `avatarUrl` that would break compression. I will focus on data validations.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now revising the `syncBladerToSupabase` function. My focus is on robust error handling. I plan to make it return a structured response, with a boolean `success` flag and an optional `error` message. This will allow for clearer logging and more informative feedback to the user. I\'ll also add a manual sync button with a status badge for real-time feedback within the Padr\303\263n.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 311280541
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
