  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Blader Updates**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on `BladersScreen.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the `Blader` addition and update flow. I\'m looking at how the new `Blader` object is created when the user submits the form. So far, I\'ve got the `id`, `name`, and `alias` parsed, but I\'m still working through how the rest of the object is created.\n\n\n**Refining Object Creation**\n\nOkay, the `Blader` object construction is really coming into focus now. I\'ve successfully traced how the `alias`, `team`, and `avatarUrl` are populated. It is very useful that it utilizes `customAvatar`, `avatarUrlInput`, and the preset values, so the user can easily select, input, or upload avatars. I see all the values are correctly trimmed, and the boolean values are as expected.\n\n\n**Improving Avatar Handling**\n\nI\'ve got it! The `BladerAvatar` component had a critical flaw in how it handled `avatarUrl`. The strict `startsWith(\'data:image\')` check completely blocked any URLs other than data URLs. Even worse, if it was empty, or failed, or a preset was used, it failed! Now, I am updating the code to correctly handle all possible URL formats, including `data:image`, `http://`, `https://`, `blob:`, `/`, and `./`. This should fix all the issues.\n\n\n**Enhancing Avatar Display**\n\nI\'ve introduced `imageError` state to `BladerAvatar` to manage image loading failures. I\'ve updated the `img` tag to use `onError` to set this state, ensuring the badge displays when an image fails to load. I\'m also now updating the avatar sizes in `BladerAvatar` to be larger and clearer on the screen. The small sizes are useful, but I will make the sizes clear to developers by making them `w-10 h-10`.\n\n\n**Investigating Database Synchronization**\n\nI\'m now diving into the database synchronization process, specifically examining `syncBladerToSupabase` in `src/lib/supabase.ts`. My initial concern is lack of user feedback upon save or error. I\'m investigating potential issues, such as the `bladers` table not existing, Supabase errors, and a mismatch in payload column names vs. the database schema. I need to make sure the column names match, especially with `registered_at` as a timestamp. I am checking the `avatar_url` length as well.\n\n\n**Expanding Sync Integration**\n\nI\'m now thinking about image compression. The current settings in `compressImage` result in relatively small JPEGs, but I want to ensure robust error handling and visual feedback for the user. I\'m especially concerned about the possibility of the user pasting a massive or invalid Base64 string. I\'m planning to enhance `syncBladerToSupabase` and `fetchBladersFromSupabase` to provide clear visual feedback on sync status. I\'m planning to introduce a real-time Supabase sync status bar in `BladersScreen.tsx`, including a status badge and a button to manually trigger a full synchronization with informative toasts on success or error. I also need to make `onSyncAllBladers` available from `App.tsx` to `BladersScreen.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 15342026
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
