    thinking: "**Defining Tournament Format**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial screen components. The first one will be `TournamentFormatScreen.tsx`. It will feature the title \"FORMATO DEL TORNEO\" and a subtitle explaining its purpose: configuring matchmaking, battle rules, victory conditions, and the tournament location. The component design will encompass a left-side layout, and from here, I can further define other aspects.\n\n\n**Elaborating Tournament Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Reglas de Combate y Formato\" main panel. I\'m structuring it with options for League/Round Robin or Direct Elimination formats. I\'m also including battle scale (1v1, 3v3, 5G), victory conditions (points-based), venue input, and participant capacity selection. There\'s a \"Save Tournament Format\" button planned. On the right, I\'m designing an \"Start Tournament\" card, featuring a rocket icon and a big \"COMENZAR TORNEO >\" button that triggers `onStartTournament()`.\n\n\n**Designing Community Configuration**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to `CommunityConfigScreen.tsx`, structuring its layout to personalize community aspects. The plan includes sections for identity, logos, cities, and organizers, with a Supabase database integration. On the left, there\'s a detailed panel for community identity and personalization with name inputs, city, organizer data, and a logo upload section. On the right, I\'m designing a card showing the community\'s current state: its name, location, and key metrics. I\'m aiming for easy, quick community customization.\n\n\n"
